  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $10.1B in federal contract spending in FY2026 to date. The Department issued 32,001 awards with an average award size of $315K, and obligations were up 5.3% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a rise to $11.6B in FY24 before a decline to $9.6B in FY25 and a partial-year rebound to $10.1B in FY26. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the single largest NAICS category in FY2026 to date at $1B, followed by Support Activities for Forestry at $890M and several food processing and construction categories. KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO is the largest vendor by obligations at $261M, with PERIMETER SOLUTIONS LP and TYSON FOODS INC. close behind at $227M and $226M respectively. The mix of spending shows heavy use of air transport, forestry support, meat and poultry processing, and computer services, reflecting both logistics and operational needs across the agency.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Agriculture's contract spending trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations rose to $11.5B in FY23 and to $11.6B in FY24, then fell to $9.6B in FY25, and reached $10.1B in FY26 to date. The Department recorded obligations up 5.3% year over year for the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Agriculture's largest procurement categories and vendors?",
        "body": "Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation leads NAICS categories at $1B, followed by Support Activities for Forestry at $890M and Animal (except Poultry) Slaughtering at $632M. KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO leads vendors at $261M, with PERIMETER SOLUTIONS LP at $227M and TYSON FOODS INC. at $226M."
      }
    ]
  },
