    {
      "q": "What does Agriculture buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Agriculture buys a mix of logistics, forestry, food processing, construction, and IT services. Top NAICS categories in FY2026 to date include Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $1B, Support Activities for Forestry at $890M, Animal (except Poultry) Slaughtering at $632M, and Computer Systems Design Services at $459M."
